# Retired launchd jobs (#432 — Option C; issue #431 decision).
#
# hub-state-check (repo drift) + skill-lint-oracle (skill-lint drift lock)
# cannot run under launchd: macOS TCC blocks launchd-spawned processes from
# reading ~/Documents (EPERM for bash, git, node AND python — #427 probe),
# and both jobs inherently read the repos there. Their work moved to
# extensions/session-checks.ts, which runs them age-gated (hub >6h, oracle
# >24h) from pi's session_start — an interactive, TCC-approved process tree.
#
# install-launchd.sh unloads + removes jobs listed here on machines that
# installed them pre-retirement. A label here must NOT also have a *.plist
# template in this directory (installer errors on the conflict).
#
# Corruption-canary + provider-latency-tripwire REMAIN launchd jobs: the
# canary watches ~/swarm (unprotected), the tripwire touches no protected
# path — both run fine under launchd.
com.eldato.hub-state-check
com.eldato.skill-lint-oracle

# ── #2048: the per-class reapers that the CONSOLIDATED pass replaced ────────────────────────────
# The Mac had four reaper triggers and four report formats, and no single answer to "is this box
# being reaped, how much did the last pass free, did it succeed" — the defect #2032 consolidated on
# the cells. `com.eldato.disk-reaper` — RENDERED by scripts/scheduled-jobs.sh from the
# `eldato-disk-reaper` record in config/scheduled-jobs.declaration, not from a template file — is now
# the ONE clock for the three disk sinks, and it runs the same `disk-reaper.sh` entry point with the
# same flags as the cells' systemd timer.
#   com.eldato.pi-cache-reap       → the pass's `uv`       class (owner: scripts/pi-cache-reap.sh)
#   com.tortoise.worktree-reaper   → the pass's `worktree` class (owner: scripts/pi-reap-worktrees.sh)
# Each retired label ran the SAME owner script the pass resolves, so nothing's delete rule changed —
# only how many clocks ran it. Both shipped unarmed (report-only), so retiring them removes no
# deletion capability; the replacement ships report-only too (the arming decision is unchanged and
# still owner-only). The tuned budgets the retired worktree job carried (#1095: 1800s pass budget,
# 120s gh timeout) moved INTO the replacement plist, or the worktree class would defer nearly every
# candidate at the 300s default.
#
# ⚠️ DELIBERATELY NOT RETIRED — neither is one of the three disk sinks, so the pass does not overlap
# them and there is exactly one owner per class:
#   com.tortoise.branch-reaper     deletes local BRANCH REFS (scripts/cleanup-stale-branches.sh)
#   com.eldato.pi-session-reaper   reaps idle pi PROCESSES (scripts/pi-reap-idle.sh)
com.eldato.pi-cache-reap
com.tortoise.worktree-reaper
